## Claim
Text: "Donald Trump, when he thinks of climate change, he says hoax. Well, guess what? Speaking of hoaxes, remember what he said about these increasing violent hurricanes and the frequency? He actually said, maybe we should detonate a nuclear bomb over the Atlantic. By the way, the same stable genius who said the biggest problem we had in the Revolutionary War is we didn’t have enough airports."
Claim author: Joe Biden
Claim date: October 30, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### Did Donald Trump publicly or privately refer to climate change as a "hoax," and if so, on what specific occasions?
Answer: Yes, Donald Trump has publicly referred to climate change as a hoax. Specifically, in November 2012, he posted a tweet stating, "The concept of global warming was created by and for the Chinese in order to make U.S. manufacturing non-competitive." While he later claimed he was joking about the Chinese connection, the source notes that "in years since [he] has continued to call global warming a hoax," though he eventually backed off the claim in a "60 Minutes" interview, stating, "I don’t think it’s a hoax."

Source URL: https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/trump-says-climate-change-not-a-hoax-but-not-sure-of-its-source

### Did Donald Trump suggest to national security or homeland security officials that the United States military should detonate a nuclear bomb over the Atlantic Ocean to disrupt hurricanes?
Answer: According to reports cited in the source, Donald Trump reportedly suggested "multiple times" in meetings with U.S. national security officials that the military should use nuclear weapons to disrupt hurricanes. Axios reported that during a White House briefing, Trump asked, "Why don't we nuke them?" and suggested dropping a bomb inside the eye of a hurricane as it moves across the Atlantic. However, Trump denied these reports, calling them "fake news" and tweeting, "I never said this."

Source URL: https://www.commondreams.org/news/2019/08/26/refusing-take-real-climate-action-trump-reportedly-suggests-using-nukes-stop

