Answer: Yes, Donald Trump blamed his July 4, 2019, gaffe about Revolutionary War airports on a malfunctioning teleprompter. He told reporters the following day that "the teleprompter went out, it went kaput" right in the middle of a sentence, adding that "it was actually hard to look at anyway because it was rain all over it."

